# core/data/talk/grammar/en/cool_insult.tlk - more replies to INSULT and MOCK (owner: TK; T5b
# package T5B-COOL). Mean is fine, cruel is not (SCRIPT_STYLE R4): the target is a hat, a walk,
# a haircut, never a body, a family, a loss or anything real. No slur, no register word. The
# sharp lines need `!kid_present`; every other line is silly enough for any room. A child
# speaker gets a cute-filtered deflection. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- INSULT -> INSULT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_back act: insult
  "Oh, you want to trade? Fine. Your jokes are stale bread."
  "Bold move. Your face is a rumour I refuse to believe."
  "You walk like a shopping trolley with one bad wheel."
  "I've met cleverer cushions. They were nicer, too."
  "You have the charm of a damp sock in a lift."
  "Wow. Did you borrow that line? It's got your fingerprints on it."
  "Your fashion sense called. It wants a lawyer."
  "You're like a candle in the wind. A bit smelly, a bit sad."
  "I'd call you a cab, but I wouldn't wish you on a cabbie."
  "Careful, you'll hurt yourself with that edge. It's made of cheese."
@rule core.insult.c_back_sharp guard: !kid_present act: insult
  "You're the human version of a Monday. Everyone's tired of you."
  "If you were any slower, you'd be a rumour."
  "Somewhere a village is missing its genius. It's okay, you're no use there."
  "You have your whole life to be wrong. Don't rush it."
  "I'd explain why you're awful, but I left my crayons at home."
  "Impressive. It takes real talent to be that loud and that empty."
@rule core.insult.c_back_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: insult
  "You've got a face like a dropped pie. Everyone looks, nobody helps."
  "That was weak. Try again. I'll wait, I've got all day."
  "Is that all? My cat insults harder. And she's a lamp."
  "Come back when you've got material. Bring a note."
@rule core.insult.c_back_polite guard: polite act: insult
  "I beg your pardon? I'd say something, but I was raised properly."
  "How rude. I'll be rude back, but with a nice napkin."
  "Well! Forgive me for saying so, but you're a bit of a lemon."
  "Goodness. And I thought we'd had such a nice start."
@rule core.insult.c_back_loud guard: loud act: insult
  "OH, IS THAT RIGHT? WELL, YOU'RE A BIG HAT WITH NO HEAD!"
  "HA! YOU CALL THAT AN INSULT? I'VE SEEN BETTER ON A LUNCH BOX!"
  "Take that back! Take it back RIGHT now! And a bit extra!"
@rule core.insult.c_back_flat guard: flat act: insult
  "That's nice. {.}You're a puddle with opinions."
  "Noted. Also, you're boring. Equal trade."
  "Sure. I'd get angry, but I'm saving it for something nice."
@rule core.insult.c_back_quirky guard: quirky act: insult
  "You're a sock! A sock in a boot, in a shoe, inside a bigger shoe!"
  "Your aura is the colour of old toast. I'm not even kidding."
  "You're like a spoon. {.}Mostly harmless, mostly in the wrong drawer."
@rule core.insult.c_back_elder guard: elder act: insult
  "In my day we called that a Tuesday. Now sit down and learn manners."
  "I've outlived better insults than that. And better people."
  "You've the manners of a goat, dear. A cheerful goat, but a goat."
@rule core.insult.c_back_rival guard: rel=rival&!kid_present act: insult
  "Of course it's you. The one splinter in my otherwise lovely day."
  "Look who found a voice. Shame it came without a brain."
  "You again. I'd say it's a pleasure, but I don't lie before lunch."
@rule core.insult.c_back_friend guard: rel=friend act: insult
  "Hey! Only I get to call you that. Rude, and accurate."
  "Oh, we're doing this? I love you, you're a goblin."
  "Okay, that was funny. I hate that it was funny."
@rule core.insult.c_back_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: insult
  "You're a poopy-head! No wait, that's rude. You're a pickle!"
  "I'm rubber, you're glue! Everything you say sticks to YOU!"
  "Hmph! You're not the boss of me. You're not even the boss of the cat."

# ---- INSULT -> COMPLAIN ------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_hurt act: complain
  "Okay, that stung. I'm putting a plaster on my feelings."
  "Wow. I came here for a nice chat and got slapped with a word."
  "That was uncalled for. I'm filing a complaint with myself."
  "Was that necessary? My self-esteem just went to lie down."
  "Hey, that's not nice. I'd cry, but I'm too stubborn."
  "Ouch. I'll be thinking about that in the shower. Thanks."
  "You could have just waved. Instead, you chose violence. Of words."
  "That's the nicest way you could've said it? Wow."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_sad guard: mood=sad act: complain
  "Today? Really? I was having a quiet little sulk, and now this."
  "I'm already low, and you came with a shovel. Thanks."
  "Please don't. I'm barely holding my smile on with tape."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_angry guard: mood=angry act: complain
  "Don't start. I'm one more rude word from a very loud afternoon."
  "Careful. I've got a temper and I know where you sleep. Roughly."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_scared guard: mood=scared act: complain
  "Not now! I'm already jumpy. I jump at my own shoes."
  "Ow! Could you be mean tomorrow? I'm busy being nervous."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_tired guard: mood=tired act: complain
  "I'm too sleepy for this. Insult me after my nap. Book a slot."
  "Mm? Was that an insult? I'll feel hurt after I wake up."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_polite guard: polite act: complain
  "That's rather unkind. I'd ask you to apologise, but I'd take tea."
  "Oh dear. I thought we were having such a civil morning."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_elder guard: elder act: complain
  "Well, I never. In my day we insulted people behind their backs."
  "Kids these days. Everyone's a poet, nobody's a gentleman."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "That's mean! I'm telling a grown-up. I'm telling TWO."
  "Hey! That hurt my feelings. They're very little feelings."
  "Not nice! Say sorry or I'm taking my ball home."
@rule core.insult.c_hurt_memory guard: fact.insulted act: complain
  "That's two today. I'm starting a tally, and I'm winning."
  "Again with the insults? You're running out of nouns."

# ---- INSULT -> DISMISS -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Mm-hm. Anything else? Besides the nonsense?"
  "I'd be hurt, but I've got a lot of better things to be."
  "That's adorable. Do you do birthdays?"
  "Say it again, but slower. I'd like to savour how little I care."
  "You've got a lot of opinions for a person with no taste."
  "Yeah, yeah. Put it in the box marked Whatever."
  "Funny. I've been called worse by weather."
  "I'm going to pretend you said something nice. Thanks!"
  "Insulted by you? Like being bitten by a sleepy kitten."
@rule core.insult.c_dismiss_flat guard: flat act: dismiss
  "Cool. {.}I'll add it to the pile. It's a big pile."
  "Okay. {.}Anyway."
  "Uh-huh. Insult received. Insult filed."
@rule core.insult.c_dismiss_easy guard: easygoing act: dismiss
  "Eh. Whatever. Mean words wash off like a rainy Tuesday."
  "No worries! I'll insult you back later. I'm on a break."
  "It's fine. I'm too comfy to be offended."
@rule core.insult.c_dismiss_serious guard: serious act: dismiss
  "That is a poor use of your breath. Please conserve it."
  "I will note your objection. In writing. And then bin it."
  "Your comment has been noted and rejected."
@rule core.insult.c_dismiss_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "Cool story. Get lost. Come back when you're interesting."
  "I don't take notes from people who dress like that."
  "Talk to the hand. It's more polite and it's got better ideas."

# ---- INSULT -> JOKE / LAUGH / TEASE / MOCK / THREATEN ---------------------------------------------
@rule core.insult.c_joke act: joke
  "Fair. I did fall for a pigeon once. Don't tell the pigeon."
  "You're right. I'm a mess. A glamorous, spilled mess."
  "I've been called a lot of things. Mostly late for dinner."
  "That's my stage name, actually. Coming soon to a bin near you."
  "I prefer 'a legend in my own lunchtime', but go on."
  "Accurate! I'll have it printed on a mug."
@rule core.insult.c_laugh act: laugh
  "Ha! That one hit. Do another, I want to see where it lands."
  "Oh, that's good. Rude, rude and good. Like soup."
  "Haha, okay, okay. I'll let that one slide. Just this once."
  "Hee! You're terrible. Let's be friends."
  "Wow, you actually went there. Respect, you maniac."
@rule core.insult.c_tease act: tease
  "Aww, you're cute when you try to be scary. Like a mad biscuit."
  "Is that your mean face? It's a bit like your regular face."
  "Look at you, being edgy. Does your mum know you're out?"
  "You're doing great, sweetie. Keep going. It's hilarious."
@rule core.insult.c_mock act: mock
  "'Oh, I'm so mean, look at me.' Nyah nyah. You sound like a kettle."
  "Ooh, 'you're a dork'. How original. Did you think that up alone?"
@rule core.insult.c_threaten act: threaten
  "Say that again and I'll feed your hat to the ducks."
  "One more word and I'll send you a strongly worded postcard."
  "Careful. I know a demon who does eviction notices. He loves them."
  "Keep going and I'll tell your mum. And the pigeons."
@rule core.insult.c_threaten_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: threaten
  "Push me. Go on. I haven't had a good scrap since Thursday."
  "I'll pop your hat so hard it'll need therapy."

# ---- MOCK -> MOCK --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.mock.c_back act: mock
  "'Ooh, I'm a mocker!' Mm, no. That's the worst impression ever."
  "Is that how I sound? It's like a goose with a head cold."
  "Okay, you try the voice. 'Hi, I'm me.' See? Terrible, you."
  "You do my walk too? It's like watching a hen cross a road."
  "Mock on, mighty mimic. I'll be over here being original."
  "That's a nice impression. Of a pudding. Is that a pudding?"
  "Hold on, I'll do you. 'Blah blah blah, look at me.' There."
  "You want to see a real mock? Watch. {.}Nope, can't compete."
@rule core.mock.c_back_quirky guard: quirky act: mock
  "Beep boop, I'm a Dr. Bloom! Look, I've got the clipboard! And no joy!"
  "Ooh, ooh, let me! 'Wah, I'm a mock.' See? It's you."
@rule core.mock.c_back_loud guard: loud act: mock
  "I DO NOT HONK LIKE THAT! {.}Okay, a little. But NOT LIKE THAT!"
  "LOOK AT ME, I'M A BIG IMPRESSION! EVERYONE CLAP FOR THE BIG GUY!"
@rule core.mock.c_complain act: complain
  "Hey, stop that. It's hard enough being me without a cover act."
  "That's not funny. {.}Okay, it's a bit funny. Stop it."
  "Quit copying me! It's creepy. You've got my elbows right."
  "I do not talk like that. My voice is much more dignified."
  "I'm very sensitive about my voice. It's a delicate instrument."
  "Don't! Everyone looks at me and I'm shy. Under the loudness."
@rule core.mock.c_complain_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "Stop copying me! Stop it, stop it! You're copying me!"
  "That's not how I talk! You're silly and wrong!"
@rule core.mock.c_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Whatever. Mimic me all day. I'll be over here, being the original."
  "Do your worst. I've got no worse to give you back."
  "That was a bad impression. Of someone I'd never be."
  "You do you. I'd say me, but you're already doing it badly."
  "Wake me when you've got your own personality."
@rule core.mock.c_joke act: joke
  "Not bad! Now do the splits. Or my sneeze, it's a sight."
  "That's a spot-on me. You've even got the hair. Where's the hair?"
  "Ha, that's uncanny. Can you do my mum? I miss her scolding."
  "Do me paying a bill! It's a horror film."
@rule core.mock.c_insult act: insult
  "You're a rubbish mimic and a worse friend. And your hat's off."
  "Copycat! Cheese-brain! I'd say more but I'm being polite."
  "You do me like a toad does an opera: loud, wrong, and confident."
@rule core.mock.c_laugh act: laugh
  "Hahaha! That's the nose, you nailed the nose! Do the ears!"
  "Oh no, it's really me. Stop, it's too good. I'm cackling."
  "Ha! I'm going to do that to someone in the pub now. Cheers."
